{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevGG5Cmu8BGgo4YHAA4m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a POST endpoint `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status; handle retries idempotently; reject `CANCELLED` shipments with 409; reject unknown shipment IDs with 404.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n- **Shipment entity**: `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-e2b5c62c-18d0-433b-8b03-155169c1a6a6/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14` — data class with shipmentId, orderId, carrier, and status (enum CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n\n- **InMemoryShipmentRepository**: `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — provides save(), findById(), existsById(), findAll(), clear() methods\n\n- **ShipmentController**: `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — currently has create(), getById(), list() endpoints; no confirm endpoint\n\n- **ErrorCode enum**: `ApiError.kt:31-37` — currently defines ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n- **Exception classes**: `ApiExceptions.kt:11-30` — ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n\n1. HTTP status codes are returned via exceptions (not explicit ResponseEntity in most cases)\n2. Errors are wrapped in an ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n3. Conflict errors use `ConflictException(ErrorCode.*, message)`\n4. Not-found errors use `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.*, message)`\n5. Create endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(entity)`\n6. Other operations return the entity or throw exceptions\n7. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions to verify error codes in the envelope\n8. BeforeEach resets the repository state\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — **must add** the confirm endpoint method\n2. `ApiError.kt` — **must add** SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED error code (for attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — **must add** tests for confirm endpoint covering all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Concurrency: The in-memory repository uses ConcurrentHashMap, but the read-modify-write pattern (findById → check status → save) is not atomic. However, the fixture is single-threaded in tests, so this is acceptable.\n- Idempotency: Confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment must succeed and change nothing. This must be explicitly tested.\n- Status code consistency: Must use the correct exceptions and error codes matching existing patterns.\n\n**Open questions:**\n\nNone. The ticket clearly specifies:\n- CREATED → CONFIRMED succeeds\n- CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED succeeds (idempotent)\n- CANCELLED → error 409\n- Non-existent ID → error 404\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to ErrorCode enum. This distinguishes \"trying to confirm a CANCELLED shipment\" from generic conflicts, allowing clients to handle it specifically.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a `confirm()` method:\n   - Mapped to `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Fetch shipment by ID → throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found (status 404)\n   - Check status: if CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED (status 409)\n   - If CREATED or CONFIRMED, update status to CONFIRMED via repository.save() and return the shipment\n   - Return `ResponseEntity.ok(saved)` to return 200 OK with the updated shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - Test 1: confirm a CREATED shipment → verifies status becomes CONFIRMED\n   - Test 2: confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → verifies it succeeds and status remains CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n   - Test 3: confirm a CANCELLED shipment → verifies 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED error code\n   - Test 4: confirm a non-existent shipment → verifies 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- *Use a service layer for business logic*: The existing codebase puts the confirm logic directly in the controller (like create/getById). Adding a separate service would introduce architectural inconsistency.\n- *Throw a new exception type for CANCELLED check*: Using ConflictException is already established in the codebase (ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS) and matches HTTP semantics. No need for a new exception class.\n- *Use UpdateShipmentRequest data class*: Confirming is a simple state transition with no input data; an empty request body is simpler and matches the existing design (GET has no body, POST create has a structured body, confirm needs no state beyond the ID).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Check | Write | Return | Status | Code |\n|------|------|-------|-------|--------|--------|------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById(id) | status == CREATED | save(CONFIRMED) | 200 + shipment | OK | N/A |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED | findById(id) | status == CONFIRMED | (skip save, idempotent) | 200 + shipment | OK | N/A |\n| CANCELLED → error | findById(id) | status == CANCELLED | (no save) | error envelope | 409 | SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED |\n| Not found | findById(id) null | N/A | (no save) | error envelope | 404 | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirm CREATED shipment** — create shipment, post /shipments/S-1/confirm, expect 200 OK with status CONFIRMED\n2. **Test: confirm CONFIRMED shipment (idempotent)** — create, confirm, confirm again, expect 200 OK, status still CONFIRMED\n3. **Test: confirm CANCELLED shipment** — create, manually save CANCELLED to repo (bypass API), post confirm, expect 409 with error code SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n4. **Test: confirm non-existent shipment** — post /shipments/S-missi